{"agent":"impl-ls-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`parse_lane_tiers` treats lane names case-sensitively, but `write_lanes` maps each lane to a file name in `.ddflow/local/`. On a case-insensitive filesystem (macOS/Windows defaults), a valid-looking config such as `mcp.lane_tools = \"impl=core,IMPL=all\"` passes validation as two distinct lanes. `write_lanes` then writes `.ddflow/local/worker-mcp-impl.json` and `.ddflow/local/worker-mcp-IMPL.json`, but those paths resolve to the same directory entry, so the first lane’s tier is silently overwritten by the second. The cleanup pass can also misreport the surviving file as stale when only the case changed, because the extracted lane name is checked against the case-sensitive `lanes` dict. Thus a lane can receive the wrong MCP tier, or `adopt` can tell the user a current lane config is stale.","digest":"bf85a7ee8556b81a","location":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:parse_lane_tiers/write_lanes","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:parse_lane_tiers/write_lanes"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11213,"diff_sha":"c4be9b411eded7c385264825079a9ee88e2094c02b030c853770b9166128ac54","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":553.5,"excluded_bytes":2676,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"b669447ecc1f0296","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LS-worker-lane-override.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T134030Z-b0387b10.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"7b9cda2e25d15eb5ebe0fd5fdc088323b526618b","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 a1cad6ddb3f53e40840dc7a5c908c86375488fb4","ddflow/config_sections/mcp.py":"100644 b0b9