{"agent":"impl-ls-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The orphan check in `write_lanes` still compares file-system lane names case-sensitively (`if lane not in lanes`) even though `parse_lane_tiers` now treats lane names as case-insensitive for file collisions. On a case-insensitive, case-preserving filesystem (macOS/Windows defaults), if the config previously had `mcp.lane_tools = \"IMPL=all\"` and is changed to `mcp.lane_tools = \"impl=all\"` with the same tier, `_write_file` sees `.ddflow/local/worker-mcp-impl.json` as the existing file `worker-mcp-IMPL.json`, returns “is current” without renaming the directory entry, and the later `local.glob(...)` still yields `worker-mcp-IMPL.json`. That extracted lane `\"IMPL\"` is not in `lanes` (`{\"impl\": \"all\"}`), so `write_lanes` also emits `worker-mcp-IMPL.json is no longer in [mcp].lane_tools (left in place)`, falsely calling the current lane file an orphan. The earlier `parse_lane_tiers` casefold fix does not answer this because it only rejects duplicate lane names within one spec, not stale existing files whose case differs from the current spec.","digest":"bf3d70c916d782b5","location":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:write_lanes","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:write_lanes"}],"chunks_total":3,"converged":{"findings_below_floor":3,"floor":"HIGH"},"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11470,"diff_sha":"0bd9262bb5d191db38e72a94c9c49997e9a714e624aa29c967c81931029168c5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":515.6,"excluded_bytes":2676,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"ac25545fe2760029","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LS-worker-lane-override.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T140402Z-ad63abcc.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"de6c0140ea51f3594934f148bc8dcf3823b7dab5","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 a1cad6ddb3f53e40840dc7a5c908c86375488fb4","ddflow/config_sections/mcp.py":"100644 b0b9a5c6aecec00480b12d2243b016d8e70bb910","ddflow/services/adopt.py":"100644 5cb97f9713860e272cf88eb9d4461e943e29a646","ddflow/services/workermcp.py":"100644 377a4fc74847d80166efa7138a2ea1c0e2c5eb64","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/mcp.md":"100644 d4e4b2b8102c51e43248ed15838e3997cca0c464","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.mcp.lane_tools.toml":"100644 dbfcddcc2d39b9553df91b070db3f8a0365e5ec0","tests/test_worker_mcp_config.py":"100644 913718053ee103e3c83971bb23effbcc2ea9c874"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":2,"rounds":2,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/workermcp.py:write_lanes"],"tree_sha":"bdb2ce6983be+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e108d1cc03fb6339cb02623c8","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":119102,"schema":1,"subject":"LS-worker-lane-override","ts":"2026-10-31T14:20:36.099828Z"}
