{"agent":"impl-ls-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"On a case-insensitive, case-preserving filesystem such as Windows, if `.ddflow/local/worker-mcp-IMPL.json` already contains exactly the text that would be written for lane `impl`, `write_lanes(repo, entry, \"impl=core\")` calls `_write_file` with the lowercase path `.ddflow/local/worker-mcp-impl.json`; `path.is_file()` and the text comparison succeed because the path resolves to the existing uppercase file, so it returns `...worker-mcp-impl.json is current` without changing the stored filename case. The stale-file scan then globs the actual name `worker-mcp-IMPL.json`, extracts lane `IMPL`, and because `lanes` is keyed by the case-sensitive key `impl`, it appends `...worker-mcp-IMPL.json is no longer in [mcp].lane_tools (left in place)`. The same active lane file is therefore reported both as current and as stale; `parse_lane_tiers` already uses `casefold()` to avoid case-insensitive collisions, but `write_lanes` does not compare stale lane names case-insensitively.","digest":"949534932ba7476a","location":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:write_lanes","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/workermcp.py:write_lanes"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11388,"diff_sha":"7cdb48de08aaf5d3bceb6c816ea661b691fac62a5c3f9567c4d76914ba5faba6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":424.2,"excluded_bytes":2676,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"c3a6b9a51988a9b4","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LS-worker-lane-override.critic.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T140306Z-362ee593.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"636da5611dcc12ff8ba649bf48e